# Scene
trueqbit with Claude (Opus 5.5), 2026-11-21: the preambles of dev/config/
re-read against irreducible-code, after trueqbit asked why the Purposes
carried prose.

# Decided
- trueqbit's wording: prologue.h "suspend, for sqlite_orm's headers, the
  compiler warnings and the macros of operating system headers"; epilogue.h
  "restore the compiler warnings and macros prologue.h suspended".
- platform.h "is used on" rather than "is built for" (header-only);
  source-layout.md "used with" likewise.
- internal_macros.h: the list of what it declares goes.
- capabilities.h (trueqbit): not "optional features" - nothing is opted in
  or out from outside; it is the one place the guards of the major features
  are visibly defined: "define, in one place, the guards of sqlite_orm's
  major features".
- config.h (lean 1): the tier list goes - it was the list of included
  headers, which each name their tier; "macros only" moves into the
  publishing paragraph. The naming sentences in the four tier headers stay
  (lean 2): a rule for whoever adds a macro, not a contents list.
- Cut as included headers or members' doing: language_features.h
  "amended where ...", stdlib_features.h "from the language features and
  compiler quirks ...", compiler_quirks.h "Keyed on ...", internal_macros.h
  "builds on config.h", platform.h "UNIX accompanies ... unknown stops".

# Discussed
- Cause, said to trueqbit: the old description comments were relabelled
  as Purposes; irreducible-code was not loaded though the local rule asks
  it; scripts/pre-commit.sh was skipped for eight commits (the memory note
  listed manual steps first). The final tree passes the script (exit 0)
  with GIT_DIR/GIT_WORK_TREE set for the worktree.
